  "notes": "BTL form 1500 (unemployment claim, 05.2026 edition, the employer's confirmation 'אישור המעסיק על תקופת ההעסקה ועל השכר'), supplied by Shlomi on 2026-10-08 as T1500.pdf; PDF page 6 of 7 (pageIndex 5), printed 'עמוד 5 מתוך 6': section I (employer details), the employee details and reason for stopping work, the pay-basis row, the notice-pay row and the employer declaration. Flat Word export with a text layer, no AcroForm, Letter page. The render is a 150 DPI pdftoppm render. Annotated from the render and the page's own primitives (pdf.js text positions and the page's painted cell interiors, raster measurement of underscore ink lines, tick combs and the ❑ checkbox ink), never from detector output. Conventions copied from btl-bl211-2015-page2/page7 and btl-1500-2026-page3/4/5/7: an underscore run is a text target 11 pt tall above the printed line, x from the first to the last underscore; a blank on an underline for a date is `date`, otherwise `text`; a tick comb is ONE target with `cells` (an 8-cell day/month/year comb is `date`, the 9-cell ID comb and the 10-cell phones are `comb`), bounded from the baseline up to the regular tick tops; a ruled cell a person writes into is kind `text`; a cell whose caption sits inside it (name, email, employer name, file number) is the writing strip beneath the caption, a cell whose caption is in its own header row (the address rows) is the whole input cell; a checkbox is the ink of the printed ❑ square, drop shadow included, and belongs to the word at its left; yes/no pairs are two independent checkboxes; a signature is a `signature` target about 17 pt tall above its line. Labels are the field's own caption, then ' / ' and its group or question. Pattern not covered by earlier truths: the three printed lines under 'הערות לסיבה להפסקת העבודה' are three text targets (one per printed line, as every underscore run is), and the two 10-cell phone combs carry a taller tick after the seventh cell which is treated as a grouping mark, not a divider (btl-bl211-2015-page2 phone rule). Not annotated: the 'לשימוש פנימי בלבד' scan box with its ID comb, document-type cells and page count, the 'חותמת קבלה' stamp box, the section badge I, the grey bars, the table caption rows, the pre-printed X marks beside the signatures, all declaration text and the footer. Checkbox bounds are the printed square without the shadow (FORM-31 convention).",
